[about]
Title=03 - Key Patterns
Intro=The rules every FileDir key follows, so a key can be guessed before it is learned: the word gives the letter, Control does, Shift asks, Shift widens, Alt Shift is a command with no control, the semicolon tags, and the function keys follow Windows.
Setup=FileDir is open on any folder.
Homework=Guess the key for Keywords, Extra Info and Rename before you look them up, then check with Control plus F1.

[step]

Say=Every key in FileDir is named for a word in its command: Control plus J is Jump, Control plus K is Keywords, Control plus C is Copy. A key never comes from the middle of a word.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Control plus a letter does something. Shift plus a letter asks something, and changes nothing: Shift plus Z says the status.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Adding Shift to a key reverses or widens it: Control plus L plays a file; Control plus Shift plus L plays every media link a page holds.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus a letter is a command with no control of its own. Alt plus a letter alone jumps to a control in a dialog.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=The function keys follow Windows and Office: F1 help, F2 rename, F3 find again, F4 pick from a list, F5 refresh, F10 the menus, F11 the version, F12 files.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=One key is FileDir's own: the semicolon tags the file you are on, and the next command acts on every tagged file. Semicolon again untags.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=The keys that explain the keys. Control plus F1 is the Key Describer: on, every key says what it does instead of doing it, the safe way to explore the keyboard. Hotkeys, in the Help menu, lists every key three ways; F1 opens the guide; and your reader's own Insert plus Tab says where you are.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=Key Describer On

[step]

Say=Control plus F1 again turns it off.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=No Key Describer

[step]

Say=The rules let a key be guessed. I say a command; the reader says the key the rules give it.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Rename the current file.
Key=
Hear=F2, or Shift plus R

[step]

Say=Copy the tagged files to another folder.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus C

[step]

Say=Move them.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus M

[step]

Say=Zip them.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus Z

[step]

Say=Tag every file.
Key=
Hear=Control plus A

[step]

Say=Untag every file.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Shift plus A

[step]

Say=Go to the parent folder.
Key=
Hear=Backspace, or Comma

[step]

Say=Keys that are the reader's are not FileDir's: anything with Insert in it belongs to the screen reader, and FileDir never uses the Insert key, so the two never collide.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=A pattern of FileDir's own: Open and Go To come in pairs. Control plus G goes to a folder in this window; Control plus O opens it in a new one. The same letter with Shift goes to the folder of the current file. Learn one pair and you have them all.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I say the key; the reader says what it does.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Control plus F1.
Key=
Hear=Key Describer
